                                                                           Python Strings

1. String
= A string is a python data type used to store text
  (character)

Example:
name = "Aman"
city= 'Delhi'


2. String Index
= String indexing is used to access individual characters.
  
~ Negative indexing starts from -1 (last character).

Example:

text = "Python"
print(text[0]) = p


3.String Slicing
= String slicing is used to extract a part of 
  a string.

Syntax:
string[start:end]

Example:
text = "Python"
print(text[0:3]) = pyt


4. String Methods

#upper() = Converts all chracters to uppercase.

 Example: print(text.upper())



#lower()
= Coverts all characters to lowercase.


Example:
text = "PYTHON"
print(text.lower())


#strip()
= Removes leading and trailing spaces.

Example:
text = "  Lnux  "
print(text.strip())

#split()
= Split a string into a list.
Example:
text = "Docker Kubernetes Jenkins"

print(text.split())


5. String Concatenation
= Concation means joining two or more strings using the 
 + operator.

Example:
first = "Hello"
second = "World"

print(first + " " + second)


6. f-Strings
= f-strings provide a clean and modern way to insert
  variables into strings.

Syntax:

f"Text {variable}"

Example:
name = "Aman"
city = "Delhi"

print(f"{name} lives in {city}")

= Aman lives in Delhi.

7. Loop with String
= A for loop can be used to ilitrate through
 every character of a string.

Example:
name = "Python"

for ch in name:
     print(ch)

